cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use EgoCraft in research or teaching, please cite it as below, and
  cite the methods behind the measures you report (the codebook and the
  draft methods section in the results ZIP list them).
title: "EgoCraft: egocentric network analysis, from interview to results"
abstract: >-
  EgoCraft collects and analyzes egocentric network data. It runs
  interviews on a laptop or an iPad, offline, with the answers kept encrypted
  on the device; imports ego, alter and tie files in common layouts; checks
  and merges them; draws each person's network; computes the measures the
  researcher chooses, including change across waves, multiplex ties and
  geography; fits regression models with alters nested in egos; and exports
  one row per ego with a codebook, a draft methods section and the Stata and
  R code that recomputes every number.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Stowell
    given-names: J.
    email: j.stowell@northeastern.edu
    affiliation: Northeastern University
repository-code: "https://github.com/nu-stats/egocraft"
